# P4NR Development Pipeline

All non-trivial work on `@plus4nodered/node-red-contrib-modbus` follows the 3-team pipeline.

## Teams

| Team | Agent | Writes to | Never touches |
|------|-------|-----------|---------------|
| 1 Spec | `p4nr-spec-author` | `docs/p4nr/capabilities/`, `docs/p4nr/plans/` | `src/`, `modbus/`, `test/` |
| 2 Review | `p4nr-spec-reviewer` | `docs/p4nr/reviews/` | Code, specs (read-only) |
| 3 Dev | `p4nr-developer` | `src/`, `test/`, locales | Without APPROVE review |

## Flow

```
Request → Team 1 (spec + plan)
       → Team 2 (review → APPROVE | REJECT)
       → GATE 1 (human approves plan)
       → Team 3 (TDD implement: RED → GREEN → build → test)
       → GATE 2 (human approves commit)
```

## Rules

1. **No code before APPROVE** in `docs/p4nr/reviews/*.review.md`
2. **REJECT** sends work back to Team 1 with listed blockers
3. **Trivial fixes** (typo, single-line obvious fix): Team 3 may skip Team 1/2 if user explicitly says so
4. After `src/` changes: always `npm run build` before testing
5. Node tests: Mocha + `node-red-node-test-helper` — not Jest
6. Use `node-red-contrib-patterns` skill for Node-RED conventions

## Orchestration Skills (ECC-compatible)

| Operation | When |
|-----------|------|
| New capability | Team 1 → Team 2 → Team 3 (maps to `orch-add-feature`) |
| Bug fix | Team 3 with regression test (maps to `orch-fix-defect`) |
| Refactor | Team 1 light plan → Team 2 → Team 3 (maps to `orch-refine-code`) |

## Artifact Index

- Specs: `docs/p4nr/capabilities/<name>.md`
- Plans: `docs/p4nr/plans/<name>.plan.md`
- Reviews: `docs/p4nr/reviews/<name>.review.md`
